### 1. Autenticação
### Login — salva os tokens para as próximas requisições
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin.teste@example.org",
  "senha": "TroqueEstaSenha123",
  "cnpj": "11222333000181"
}
> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken); client.global.set("usuarioId", response.body.usuarioId); %}

### Ver dados do token autenticado
GET http://localhost:8080/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Renovar access token
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}
> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken); %}

### Alterar senha (troque os valores; exige a senha atual)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/alterar-senha
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senhaAtual": "TroqueEstaSenha123",
  "novaSenha": "NovaSenhaTeste123",
  "confirmarNovaSenha": "NovaSenhaTeste123"
}

### Logout — invalida o refresh token usado
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}
